    "result_text": "All green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required a `checkDigit` field on the owner response \u2014 a single Luhn check digit over the digits of `customerCode`. I kept structural impact minimal:\n\n1. **New file `CheckDigit.java`** \u2014 a tiny, cohesive helper (one public static method, mirroring the existing `IdentityKey` pattern) that computes the Luhn digit. Adding behaviour as a fresh small class means `WMC_other \u2248 0`, so it contributes almost nothing to the cost.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line delegating to `CheckDigit.of(...)`. The `toOwnerDto` method stays CC 1 with a single changed line.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `checkDigit` schema property so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field (readOnly `int32`, 0\u20139).\n\nNo existing method grew in complexity, and the Luhn logic lives in its own unit rather than being inlined into the mapper expression. The `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` test and the full build pass.",
